    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0383" n="290" xml:id="pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.51B861/127: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-09T18:00:00-04:00">September 9, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>199. Embassy’s 193, August 29, 5 p.m. Banking representatives of Province advise
                    that negotiations are still continuing although at the moment slowly, due partly
                    to preoccupation of Provincial Minister of Finance, now Acting Governor, with
                    other matters.</p>
                <p>While at Rosario de la Frontera, I handed the Minister for Foreign Affairs a copy
                    of the Embassy’s letter dated August 27 to the Under Secretary for Foreign
                    Affairs. I urged on him that while discussions were going on the provincial
                    authorities should take no unilateral action. Saavedra Lamas stated that he felt
                    that this attitude was eminently just and that, upon his return to Buenos Aires
                    during the present week, he would take up the matter with President Justo. He
                    said he hoped that nothing on the subject would get into the newspapers as it
                    would do harm.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
